IN THE FIRST QUARTER OF 2020 BUT THAT DATES WERE FLUID. CHASE HAS ALSO PROMISED THAT 20%, OR 10, OF ITS NEW BRANCHES WILL BE IN LOW-TO-MODERATE INCOME NEIGHBORHOODS. IT APPEARS TO BE WELL ON ITS WAY TO MEETING THAT THRESHOLD, WITH EXISTING LOCATIONS IN CAMDEN, UPPER DARBY AND GRAYS FERRY, THE ONE COMING IN NORTH PHILADELPHIA AND OTHERS IN THE WORKS IN KENSINGTON, PORT RICHMOND, WEST PHILADELPHIA AND ISLAND AVENUE NEAR PHILADELPHIA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT.'}